ocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hello @acetcom ,\r\n\r\nI am using the code from tag v2.3.0, where SGWC crashes randomly when placing either multiple calls or when disconnecting a single VoLTE call. I am attaching a trace containing the following scenario\r\n\r\n1. Register two UEs with IMS\r\n2. Place a call\r\n3. Disconnect the call\r\n4. SGWC crashes (random)\r\n\r\n[sgwc_crash_epc.zip](https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/files/6817215/sgwc_crash_epc.zip)\r\n\r\nFollowing is the backtrace on SGWC long with some logs\r\n[sgwc_backtrace_log.txt](https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/files/6817231/sgwc_backtrace_log.txt)\r\n\r\nWhile debugging based on the backtrace and logs I found some issue in the following code, where variable 'sess' is being used in ogs_list_for_each, but 'sess' is a parameter passed to sgwc_sxa_handle_session_modification_response function and being overwritten in ogs_list_for_each. Please correct me if I got this wrong. There are other places in the sgwc_sxa_handle_session_modification_response function where sess is overwritten \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/blob/4667b99c922a89399ccb22dc27ae4bd64d7fdcf3/src/sgwc/sxa-handler.c#L989","closed_by":{"login":"herlesupreeth","id":4115839,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTU4Mzk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4115839?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/herlesupreeth","html_url":"https://github.com/herlesupreeth","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/herlesupreeth/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/herlesupreeth/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/herlesupreeth/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/herlesupreeth/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/herlesupreeth/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/herlesupreeth/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/herlesupreeth/repos","events_ur